The 74LS90 is a 14-pin IC. Here’s a breakdown of its pin configuration:
Pin Configuration for 74LS90 (Decade Counter)

    Pin 1 (NC): Not connected.
    Pin 2 (R1): Reset 1 - Used for resetting the counter.
    Pin 3 (R2): Reset 2 - Used with Pin 2 to reset the counter.
    Pin 4 (NC): Not connected.
    Pin 5 (Vcc): Connects to the positive power supply (typically 5V).
    Pin 6 (NC): Not connected.
    Pin 7 (GND): Ground - Connects to the ground of the circuit.
    Pin 8 (Q2): Output - Second bit of the binary count.
    Pin 9 (Q1): Output - First bit of the binary count.
    Pin 10 (GND): Ground.
    Pin 11 (Q3): Output - Third bit of the binary count.
    Pin 12 (Q0): Output - Least significant bit (LSB) of the binary count.
    Pin 13 (Clock B): Secondary clock input.
    Pin 14 (Clock A): Primary clock input - Often used as the main clock input to increment the counter.

This configuration allows the 74LS90 to be used in various counting and timing applications. For our project, the main pins of interest are Clock A (Pin 14) to increment the count, Q0-Q3 (Pins 8, 9, 11, and 12) for output, and Reset (Pins 2 and 3) to reset the counter.
